From e642d93e64b6f9ef2b6d9e1752a57038c7cffafc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:49:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 098/274] Sparse-MLA metadata: the window metadata and main
 page table in one launch

The TileLang window and page kernels were 0.2-0.4 us slower than Triton's pair
under decode graphs (T1 window 1); the decode metadata writes both for the same
rows back to back. decode_metadata_kernel writes a row's window metadata and its
main page table in one launch (the window logic shared with chunk_kernel as a
macro); index pages keep the standalone kernel.

(cherry picked from commit b1741ef1ec4bcd5d496c1371140f073a5052da2d)

